<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Union labels Amplats a &quot;hostile employer&quot;.</title>
<headline>Union labels Amplats a &quot;hostile employer&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Union of Mineworkers (NUM) said on Friday it had identified Anglo American Platinum Corp Ltd as a &quot;hostile employer&quot; and said the company would be handled as such.  </p>
<p>It attacked the firm for the handling of its application for a court interdict to halt a strike at its Rustenburg Platinum Mine this week.</p>
<p>The wildcat strike by 4,600 workers, lasting just over two days, affected 15 percent of production at the Rustenburg mine.  </p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
